    <article class="content-block">
      <p class="label">Blog</p>
      <h1>Research methodology reflections</h1>
      <p>Good research methods are not chosen for elegance alone. They are chosen to answer a decision, illuminate a gap, or surface the conditions under which a service or product can work.</p>
      <p>In practice, that means combining interviews, observations, benchmarking, card sorts, surveys, and journey mapping in ways that reflect both the customer experience and the operational system behind it.</p>
      <p>What matters most is not the method itself, but whether the evidence is credible, actionable, and connected to the actual work of changing an experience.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
